  E'His feed is a steady, almost meditative stream of Radhanagar sunsets, Havelock low-tide pools, Port Blair monsoon skies and Neil Cove blues, often cut to music. It\'s the kind of account that does what local creators do best - it doesn\'t treat the islands like a \'destination\', it treats them like a hometown that happens to look like this. For a lot of young Indians, his reels are the first time the Andamans show up on their phone without a packaged \'Top 10 things to do\' voiceover.',
  E'His feed is a steady, almost meditative stream of Radhanagar sunsets, Havelock low-tide pools, Port Blair monsoon skies and Neil Cove blues, often cut to music. It\'s the kind of account that does what local creators do best - it doesn\'t treat the islands like a \'destination\', it treats them like a hometown that happens to look like this. For a lot of young Indians, his reels are the first time the Andamans show up on their phone without a packaged \'Top 10 things to do\' voiceover.\n\nA small personal note - I know Shiv, and what most of his audience doesn\'t see is that the man can *dance*. His game is genuinely strong on the floor, and because he DJs too, the music, the cuts and the body language in his reels all click together. Brands have caught on - he\'s already collaborated with the likes of Goibibo on island showcases ([Mark Bay Beach reel](https://www.instagram.com/goibibo/reel/C8BltcgBq_8/)) - but the best version of him is still the one mid-set, doing his thing.'
)
